<title>USA: National-Standard to open new filter plant.</title>
<headline>National-Standard to open new filter plant.</headline>
<dateline>NILES, Mich. 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>National-Standard Co said Monday it would open a new facility by October 1 to produce filters for air bags fitted into cars and trucks.</p>
<p>The plant, located in Moses Lake, Wash., would be the company's sixth for producing filtration materials for air bags. The company acquired the manufacturing machinery from Olin Air Bag Products, also of Moses Lake.</p>
<p>The facility will initially employ 12 to 20 people.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
